# Changelog
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).


## [2.0.1] - 2026-04-12

### Fixed

- Fixes to WatneyAstrometry.ImageReaders: 8-bit monochrome PNG images had
  mistakenly set the BPP in the image metadata to 16 while it should have been
  8. This had caused exceptions when being processed by the DefaultStarDetector
  for example.
- CommonFormatsImageReader.IsSupported() was throwing exceptions after 2.0.0
  as ImageSharp API had changed and was throwing NotSupportedException for
  unsupported formats. This has now been fixed and the method will never
  throw again, returning false when the format is not supported.



## [2.0.0] - 2026-03-05

### Changed

- The desktop app is now upgraded to Avalonia 11.3 and .NET 10.0.

- WatneyAstrometry.Core has been updated with significant performance
  improvements. Performance boosts were observed to have 61% reduction
  in blind solve times in average, sometimes even better.



## [1.0.3] - 2023-07-04

### Changed

- WatneyAstrometry.Core updated to v1.2.3 which introduces improved match 
  filtering. This mainly affects images with large field radiuses and
  massive amounts of stars visible, improving the solve accuracy. 
  Fields with tens of thousands of stars should now solve with better
  accuracy.



## [1.0.2] - 2023-01-21

### Added

- A setting to allow limiting how many threads the solver can use.
  It defaults to CPU logical core count - 1.



## [1.0.1] - 2022-08-23

### Fixed

- Dialogs now open properly at the center of their owner windows.

- The version string is now properly displayed in the main window title
  in Linux.
  
- Latest used paths in file open dialogs are persisted and saved to a 
  config file.



## [1.0.0] - 2022-08-21

### Initial release of Watney Astrometry Desktop

- Release numbering will be independent from WatneyAstrometry.Core
  versioning.
- Additional version build information will be appended to identify
  the build date and source git commit.


